{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"carried_from":"prior finding 1","checklist_item":"- [ ] Decide whether a non-dict `bindings`/`reverse` in a well-formed bindings.json should raise an operational (exit-2) error rather than be silently coerced to empty and reported clean.","criteria":["edge-cases","correctness"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:205: `    if not isinstance(bindings, dict):`","src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:206: `        bindings = {}`","src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:207-208 coerce a non-dict `reverse` to `{}` likewise","release-notes claim: 'malformed JSON is an operational exit 2' and 'None of these failures may be reported as a clean store' — but a valid top-level object with a non-dict `bindings`/`reverse` bypasses `_read_integrity_store`'s object check and yields an empty (clean) integrity list"],"finding":"`audit_store_integrity` silently coerces a non-dict `bindings` or `reverse` value (e.g. a list, string, number, or null) to an empty dict, so a structurally corrupt bindings.json whose top level is a valid object but whose index sub-values are malformed produces an empty `store_integrity` (a clean audit) instead of an operational exit-2 or a finding. This conflicts with the change's stated fail-closed intent for malformed store state.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:203","norm_id":"n8061c1bce8598928","priority":0.2571,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Raise `_integrity_error(...)` when `store` contains a `bindings`/`reverse` key whose value is present but not a dict, instead of coe